& [DictatedConcept]
  + make an attention signal that diffuses decays and reverberates to infer the next step and try to restore what was forgotten
  + hold one function that can restore state and another whose signal decays while the decayed signal can still lead back to current state
  + reduce the live scope of attention while retaining the terms needed to recover the wider state
  + over time the retained terms become a story of the experience within that inference window and may be saved as narrative
  + test whether moment-by-moment attention can be tracked and narrated and whether current state can be faithfully restored from the compressed signal

& [SelectedNames]
  + ReverberantAttentionTrace is the small source-bound live signal projected into the current inference window
  + RecoverabilityEnvelope is the larger exact state that the trace can address through retained identities pointers and restoration rules
  + RestorationCheckpoint is the content-addressed exact state needed to resume without treating recollection as fact
  + AnchorCheck compares a reconstructed working state with governing sources open obligations latest receipts and the unresolved frontier
  + NarrativeProjection renders attributed semantic events into a human-readable account without replacing the exact event ledger

& [FourLayerModel]
  + ActiveTrace contains a bounded set of LookaheadStitch identities subject distinctions current transform completion cue and restoration pointers
  + RestorationCheckpoint retains exact source identities requirements constraints denials plan frontier artifacts receipts and causal event coordinates outside the model context
  + Reverberation uses the surviving trace and checkpoint pointers to request bounded reconstruction of the next working state then verifies it before use
  + NarrativeProjection converts admitted observations decisions transforms receipts decay refresh invalidation release and anchor outcomes into an attributed story

& [DecayAndRefresh]
  + salience decays by explicit deterministic policy over semantic events or admitted clocks rather than by an inaccessible feeling inside the model
  + mandatory governing anchors restoration pointers unresolved obligations and safety denials do not decay below their declared floor while their scope remains active
  + a trace item refreshes only through a cited observation decision receipt dependency use or explicit operator action
  + fulfilled invalidated superseded or out-of-scope items leave the active trace while their immutable ledger history remains
  + decay is recorded so the system can distinguish information deliberately released from information accidentally omitted

& [FunctionalSeparation]
  + DecayController is a deterministic function that scores salience applies floors expires items and emits a complete decay refresh and release receipt
  + ReconstructionAdapter may use inference to propose a compact working-state reconstruction from trace checkpoint and current observation
  + AnchorVerifier deterministically checks identities mandatory coverage causal receipt order and unresolved-frontier conservation before the proposed state is admitted
  + these are functional roles and do not require two language models; later governed experiments may distribute them across models or processes

& [RecoverabilityClaimBoundary]
  + a compressed trace cannot universally restore arbitrary information after the exact information has been destroyed
  + faithful restoration is possible only when the external checkpoint and event ledger retain sufficient exact state and the trace preserves an unambiguous route to it
  + the trace may be a scope-specific sufficient recovery key but is not assumed to be a lossless encoding of the whole experience
  + semantic reconstruction may summarize or organize exact state but may not invent missing observations receipts authority or causal history
  + if more than one state fits the retained evidence the result is underdetermined and requires more source material or operator judgment

& [AnchorCheck]
  + compare the active subject and scope with the declared source authority and current plan coordinate
  + require every nondecaying governing anchor denial and open requirement that applies at the reconstruction point
  + verify the latest accepted receipts artifact identities and causal predecessor relation
  + conserve the unresolved frontier and make newly resolved or newly opened obligations explicit
  + return anchored when exact correspondence and mandatory coverage hold drifted when a contradiction or lost obligation is proved and underdetermined when retained evidence cannot select one state
  + drifted and underdetermined states may be inspected but may not silently continue autonomous work

& [MomentByMomentMeaning]
  + moment means an explicit admitted semantic event such as observation intent decision transform tool request tool receipt gate result commit publication decay refresh or release
  + the event ledger records inputs source bindings actor operation result identity causal predecessor and unresolved effect for each admitted event
  + the proposal does not record hidden chain of thought private token-by-token cognition logits attention heads K/V cache or unverifiable internal states
  + a model may provide a concise public rationale or proposed narrative sentence but the ledger and receipts determine what actually occurred

& [NarrativeFormation]
  + NarrativeProjection selects ledger events within one subject scope and time or causal interval
  + it explains the active intention governing constraints material decisions accepted operations evidence unresolved frontier and how attention items decayed refreshed or reentered
  + every narrative statement points to ledger events sources receipts or is marked interpretation
  + the narrative can help a later agent recover the frame of mind while exact checkpoints and element histories restore machine-verifiable state
  + different narrative projections may serve operator review technical reentry or audit without changing the underlying event history

& [PowerAndExperimentDirection]
  + the hypothesis is that a small live attention trace plus exact recoverability envelope can reduce repeated context load while retaining auditable continuity
  + compare full-context replay static summary reverberant trace with checkpoint and trace without checkpoint under identical tasks providers model parameters tools and budgets
  + measure reconstruction coverage anchor outcome lost obligations unsupported additions tokens context bytes calls reads time to correct next action and accepted closure
  + adversarial cases include stale pointers conflicting receipts ambiguous state missing mandatory anchors premature decay poisoned narrative and a plausible but false reconstruction
  + no compression fidelity continuity speed or attention-widening benefit is accepted without provider-free structural tests and later separately governed live evidence

& [RelationshipToCompiledLookahead]
  + LookaheadStitch supplies compact forward trajectory cues while ReverberantAttentionTrace governs which stitches and restoration pointers remain active across semantic events
  + StitchSelector may propose the minimal active term set but cannot override mandatory retention floors or AnchorCheck
  + the combined image is a small active attention window inside a larger externally recoverable state rather than a larger hidden model context

& [AuthorityBoundary]
  + this snapshot authorizes exact source custody and later SJS processing only
  + no canonical schema decay equation retention floor reconstruction algorithm narrative compiler satisfaction signature Rust implementation provider call model distribution autonomous execution workspace mutation remote host FPGA Minecraft physical effect or performance claim is authorized
